capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1793723480,"sha":"4ce79094aaf3cf8753bb438a17cd3d9b40afa02a","subject":"docs(memory): add Period Note and Stats Strip glossary terms"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"235e63df7e2391d204a609b16f7434d54d37a33e1e93450813cca1d9c7791619","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-gh.1--plan/commits.json","size_bytes":238},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"3942241a63c5de53df93bede886ed35a51f8b6a33d5883d819c898d7dd34f408","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-gh.1--plan/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":83},"meta":{"digest":"371cc0a1c26d7453d8c2b4976469568a01337c0d10ab45ffbe391bc4d07633f5","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-gh.1--plan/meta.json","size_bytes":9117},"prompt":{"digest":"b937b02f6a9fcde4d49fe4a9ef832981f336a7cae62a1427c30f5ab8746f5b08","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-gh.1--plan/prompt.md","size_bytes":183},"state":{"digest":"0b9766ea6eae66ba28e1e6d243ec092b053db1a2cacf5f689e82e7cc8e27e955","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-gh.1--plan/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-gh.1--plan","local_name":"bob-cli-gh.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-gh","agent_clan_generation":"20261103105651","agent_session":"bob-cli-gh.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"bob-cli-gh.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-gh[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Period notes that add up: a whole-ISO-week Week → Quarter → Year → [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]All-time tree with stats strips, parts tables, and reviews Bryan [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]closes[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every daily note's parent is its ISO week note, and the tree climbs[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]week → quarter → year → all_time → org with no dangling links. bob [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]creates each period note ahead of time from a deterministic [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]scaffold and never edits a note it did not just create. Every week,[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]quarter, year, and all-time note opens with a live stats strip — [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the Day strip's family: the same five facts as period totals, a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]typical line, root and type lanes, and a parts row of its child [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]periods — and a live parts table that summarizes each child [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]automatically, with or without an agent. Each note carries [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]complete, versioned agent instructions, so \"Update [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]2026/2026-W45.md\" is a whole prompt: agents take every number from [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`bob periods brief` and save only through `bob periods draft`, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]which never overwrites Bryan's edits. gtd_daily.md runs a Monday [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]weekly review plus calendar-anchored quarterly and yearly reviews, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and the glossary and decision records name the new pieces.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]9[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]period_notes_and_stats_strips.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/period_notes_and_stats_strips.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-gh[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-gh/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Glossary strands and decision records[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]vocab[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]vocab: add the Stats Strip and Period Note glossary strands, reword Day [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Strip as the daily member of the stats-strip family, write the three [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]period decision records, and republish memory.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Period calendar, scaffolds, note parser, and bob periods [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]ensure/list[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core: a new `periods` module in bob-cli with the ISO period calendar, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ids, paths, labels, the four deterministic scaffolds (with v1 agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]callouts), the note-anatomy parser and review-state machine, create-only[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`bob periods ensure` with one-week look-ahead, a basic `bob periods [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list`, CLI wiring, and the first `docs/periods.md`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Period report — bob periods show and period stats ranges[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]report[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]report: `bob periods show` (human and JSON) with so-far facts that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]include today, same-kind typical lines, folded lanes, strip columns, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parts-table children with review state, Headline, and an automatic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]\"mostly\" line; plus `bob stats -r <period>` and `-g quarter`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Vault adoption — bob periods migrate, problems report, nightly[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]check[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]migrate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate: `bob periods migrate` (dry run by default, one verified commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with `-a`) that creates the ISO-2026 tree, adopts 2026.md, re-parents [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]year notes and daily notes, and adds the week nav link; `bob periods [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]list -p` problems; and a report-only nightly step.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Agent reviews — bob periods brief, draft, and instruction [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]refresh[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]reviews[dim] · [dim][/dim]after report[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reviews: the deterministic, versioned `bob periods brief` bundle for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]weeks, quarters, and years; `bob periods draft` with Headline and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]word-cap validation and the empty/drafted/edited/reflected guard; and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`bob periods ensure -R` to refresh agent callouts.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Period-note creation hook, open-week command, and agent [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]callout style[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]hook[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]hook: bob-ledger-tools runs `bob periods ensure` on daily-note creation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and once per local day, gated on all_time.md; adds an \"Open this week's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]note\" command; and styles `[!agent]` callouts as one quiet folded line.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The period stats strip in bob-ledger-tools, week member first[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]strip[dim] · [dim][/dim]after report[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]strip: the `bob-stats-strip` fence and the shared period strip (facts, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]typical line, meta, lanes) built on the Day strip components, the week [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]parts row of seven day columns, interactions and keyboard, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`openStatsForPeriod`, caching and refresh, preview fixtures, and tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Quarter, year, and all-time strips plus the bob-period-parts [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]table[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]parts[dim] · [dim][/dim]after strip[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]parts: the quarter (week columns, month ticks), year (week columns in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]quarter groups), and all-time (quarter columns in year groups) parts [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows, and the live `bob-period-parts` table for every kind, with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]previews, tests, and plugin docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Vault rollout, review rituals, and live verification[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rollout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after vocab, migrate, reviews, hook, parts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rollout: install bob and the plugins, verify the recurrence strings, run[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the migration dry run and then apply it, switch the daily template, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retire the monthly and yearly templates, update day.md, journal.md, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]org.md, and gtd_daily.md, pilot drafts, capture screenshots, and file [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the automation follow-up.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-gh","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-gh.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","role_suffix":"plan",